{
  "schema_version": "1.7.0",
  "id": "USN-8913-1",
  "summary": "libx11 vulnerabilities",
  "details": "Adam Bedard discovered that libx11 incorrectly handled certain XKB keyboard\nmap replies. If a user were tricked into connecting to a malicious X\nserver, a remote attacker could possibly use this issue to cause libx11 to\ncrash, resulting in a denial of service, or possibly execute arbitrary\ncode. (CVE-2026-88806)\n\nIt was discovered that libx11 incorrectly handled certain X Input Method\n(XIM) messages. If a user were tricked into connecting to a malicious X\nserver, a remote attacker could possibly use these issues to cause libx11\nto crash, resulting in a denial of service. (CVE-2026-94283,\nCVE-2026-94284)\n\nIt was discovered that libx11 incorrectly handled converting certain\nmultibyte text. An attacker could possibly use this issue to cause libx11\nto crash, resulting in a denial of service. (CVE-2026-94285)",
  "aliases": [],
